  "question": "Why do the largest health systems in the connectivity ledger show zero endpoints?",
  "answer": "The zero is not an absence. 6 of 6 systems publish a FHIR endpoint in Epic's brand file, and the NDH itself carries that endpoint for 5. For 5 of those 5, every copy has either no managingOrganization or one holding no practitioner roles in the state. In 6 of 6 no member organization carries partOf, and in 6 of 6 the vendor publishes no member organization's NPI. The systems hold 21,963 distinct clinicians (the ledger's per-system counts sum practitioner-organization links). Through a member organization or CMS enrollment, the same tiers the ledger's practitioner funnel accepts, 13,755 of them already reach an endpoint (a lower bound on what the funnel credits them, since it also counts non-member organizations): 0 through the NDH or a vendor-published NPI, the only links the system rollup counts, 10,718 through name or brand resolution (H53) and 3,037 through CMS enrollment.",
